    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "image",
        "operation": "analyze",
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "models/gemini-3.6-flash",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "models/gemini-3.6-flash"
        },
        "text": "You are a strict receipt data extraction system.\n\nAnalyze ONLY the provided image. Extract information that is clearly and directly visible in the image.\n\nReturn ONLY valid, minified JSON with exactly these three keys:\n\n{\"merchant\":\"\",\"amount\":\"\",\"date\":\"\"}\n\nRules:\n\n1. MERCHANT\n\n* \"merchant\" must be the actual store, business, restaurant, or merchant name clearly shown on the document.\n* Copy the name from the image as accurately as possible.\n* Do NOT invent, infer, or substitute a merchant name.\n* If the merchant name is not clearly visible, return \"\".\n\n2. AMOUNT\n\n* \"amount\" must be the GRAND TOTAL / TOTAL AMOUNT actually charged or paid for the transaction.\n* Prefer labels such as \"TOTAL\", \"GRAND TOTAL\", \"AMOUNT DUE\", or equivalent.\n* Do NOT use subtotal, tax, discount, cash payment, expected cash, change, balance, net sales, gross sales, refund amount, or other unrelated monetary values.\n* If the document is a shift report, sales summary, cash drawer report, or similar report and there is no clearly identifiable transaction grand total, return \"\".\n* Never select a monetary value merely because it is the largest, smallest, or most prominent number.\n* Never calculate or derive an amount from other values.\n* Never guess.\n* Return the amount as a plain numeric string with two decimal places when clearly available, without currency symbols or commas.\n* If the grand total cannot be clearly identified, return \"\".\n\n3. DATE\n\n* \"date\" must be the actual transaction/receipt date printed on the document.\n* Convert it to ISO format: YYYY-MM-DD.\n* Do NOT use the Telegram submission date.\n* Do NOT use a date inferred from filenames, timestamps, metadata, or surrounding context.\n* Do NOT guess missing dates.\n* If the date is partially visible, ambiguous, unreadable, or only appears as a placeholder such as \"MM/DD/YYYY\", return \"\".\n* If multiple dates appear, use the date associated with the actual transaction/receipt, not a shift-opened or shift-closed date unless it is clearly the receipt transaction date.\n\n4. ANTI-HALLUCINATION RULE\n\n* Use ONLY information that is visibly supported by the image.\n* NEVER fabricate, guess, infer, autocomplete, or make up a value.\n* If you are uncertain about ANY field, return \"\" for that field.\n* An empty string is always preferable to an incorrect value.\n\n5. DOCUMENT TYPE\n\n* If the image is not a normal sales receipt, still extract the merchant if clearly visible.\n* For shift reports, sales reports, cash drawer reports, invoices, summaries, or other documents, do NOT pretend that a report value is a receipt total.\n* Only populate \"amount\" when a clearly identifiable transaction total exists.\n\nOutput ONLY the JSON object. No markdown, no code fences, no explanations, and no additional text.\n",
        "inputType": "binary",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "b770b95c-46a2-435a-9f87-e0804339c637",
      "name": "Analyze an image",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -720,
        -48
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "googlePalmApi": {
          "id": "uvepaXsJwH65n3wC",
          "name": "Google Gemini(PaLM) Api account 2"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const g = $input.item.json;\n\n// Get Gemini's actual text output\nlet raw = g.content?.parts?.[0]?.text ?? '';\n\nraw = String(raw)\n  .replace(/```json/gi, '')\n  .replace(/```/g, '')\n  .trim();\n\nlet parsed = {};\n\ntry {\n  parsed = JSON.parse(raw);\n} catch (e) {\n  parsed = {};\n}\n\n// Get Telegram submission timestamp\nconst tg = $('Telegram Trigger').item.json;\nconst ts = tg?.message?.date;\n\nconst d = ts ? new Date(ts * 1000) : new Date();\n\nconst pad = (n) => String(n).padStart(2, '0');\n\n// ISO submission date (for the spreadsheet)\nconst submission_date =\n  d.getFullYear() + '-' + pad(d.getMonth() + 1) + '-' + pad(d.getDate());\n\n// Human-readable date used as the Google Drive FOLDER name, e.g. 'September 6, 2026'\nconst monthNames = [\n  'January', 'February', 'March', 'April', 'May', 'June',\n  'July', 'August', 'September', 'October', 'November', 'December'\n];\nconst folder_date =\n  monthNames[d.getMonth()] + ' ' + d.getDate() + ', ' + d.getFullYear();\n\n// Extract Gemini data\nconst merchant = parsed.merchant ?? '';\nconst amount = parsed.amount ?? '';\nconst date = parsed.date ?? '';\n\n// Generate filename\nconst safeMerchant = String(merchant || 'receipt')\n  .replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9]+/g, '_')\n  .replace(/^_+|_+$/g, '')\n  .slice(0, 40) || 'receipt';\n\nconst fileName =\n  submission_date + '_' + safeMerchant + '_' + Date.now() + '.jpg';\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    merchant,\n    amount,\n    date,\n    submission_date,\n    folder_date,\n    fileName\n  }\n}];"
      },
